  "about": "The world's named landmarks and the cells each covers (docs/design/world-tools.md G1; Places.cs): what the rules MCP's places() and here() read, and what a look's \"where\" names. Read-only: mods can't change them. Cells are grid cells (y grows south). An entry with \"generated\": true is made from the world file in its \"from\" (villages.json, gauntlet.json, golf.json, puzzles.json, and land.json's water bodies by the \"generate\" settings), so don't edit it: change that file and regenerate (PLACES_OUT=1 dotnet test core --filter PlacesFileIsUpToDate). The rest are written by hand, saying where they came from. Shapes: \"area\" [x0, y0, x1, y1] (corners inclusive), \"line\" points with a \"width\" in cells, \"circle\" {at, radius}, \"rows\" [y, x0, x1, ...] spans.",
